single-1  | entrypoint: first-boot stages: [1/3] docker/prepare.sh [2/3] verify.sh --no-server [3/3] start_qwen.sh (single)
single-1  | entrypoint: stage 1 is minutes on first boot (download + requantize), seconds once prepared
single-1  | entrypoint: use log timestamps as the elapsed timer; total first boot can exceed 30 min
single-1  | [effective-config] MODE=single
single-1  | [effective-config] CTX=fast SPEC=dflash2
single-1  | [effective-config] MODEL=/app/models/Qwen3.8-27B-W4A16-AutoRound-fast PORT=18020
single-1  | [effective-config] MAX_LEN=65536 MAX_SEQS=16
single-1  | [effective-config] VLLM_API_KEY=unset api_key.txt=absent
single-1  | [start_qwen] note: the pinned pool holds about 6 resident requests on short (~1k-token) prompts and about 1 at MAX_LEN=65536, at DFLASH_TOKENS=7 (one request needs 54+2*ceil(ctx/864) of the pool's 382 pages, so context is what moves it); MAX_SEQS=16 admits more than that and the rest queue.
